"Plotbook\u2019s setup package is ready for review. It covers all five first-version outcomes: applications, allocation and waiting lists, gardeners\u2019 allocation details, problem reporting, and the coordinator\u2019s 40-plot map. Payments and tool lending remain deferred.\n\nThe independent review found no blocking gaps. I incorporated coordinator entry of previous-season holdings, deterministic application ordering, cutoff-boundary tests, and explicit large-text/plain-language checks.\n\nPhases are milestones; tickets are specific work items. The labels below are provisional.\n\n| Milestone | Tickets and dependencies |\n|---|---|\n| **Decisions and prototype** | **A1:** Choose stack/deployment. **A2:** Decide sign-in and household identity. **A3:** Confirm cutoff/date details and priority versus waiting-list handling. **A4:** Decide report notifications. **A5:** Prototype the phone journeys and plot layout. **A6:** Owner reviews prototype; depends on A5. |\n| **Applications and privacy** | **B1:** Establish application scaffold and verification tooling; depends on A1. **B2:** Season, household and plot records, including coordinator entry of previous-season holdings; depends on B1 and relevant A3 decisions. **B3:** Sign-in, roles and coordinator-only contact access; depends on A2/B2. **B4:** Application submission and coordinator review; depends on B3/A6. **B5:** Owner demonstrates intake and privacy; depends on B4. |\n| **Allocation and map** | **C1:** Testable allocation rules and protection against duplicate holdings; depends on B2/A3. **C2:** Coordinator allocation and chronological waiting list; depends on C1/B4. **C3:** Gardener allocation and season dates; depends on C2. **C4:** Coordinator\u2019s 40-plot grid with usable phone presentation; depends on C2/A6. **C5:** Owner reviews allocation, queue and map; depends on C3/C4. |\n| **Problems and acceptance** | **D1:** Gardener reports a problem with their allocated plot; depends on C3. **D2:** Coordinator views and resolves reports; depends on D1. **D3:** Integrated rule, privacy, recovery and accessibility verification; depends on B5/C5/D2. **D4:** Owner accepts the first version against the brief; depends on D3. |\n\nEach implementation ticket will include its brief reference, scope, observable acceptance criteria, failure/empty/loading/recovery behaviour, verification, dependencies and assumptions.\n\nUnanswered choices remain owner decisions; affected implementation waits for them. Notifications require a decision before any delivery mechanism is added. Checkpoints are ordinary tickets\u2014the tool does **not** enforce owner approval when closing them.\n\nApproval also covers:\n\n- **Project:** Plotbook; initially `generic`, language undecided.\n- **Governance:** `AGENTS.md`, domain and TDD rules in `RULES.md`, and the standard `REVIEW.md` contract.\n- **Quality:** Full pipeline, justified by allocation rules and privacy requirements. `WRITE_TESTS`, `TEST`, `BUILD` and `VERIFY` explicitly disabled until actual commands are established; commands remain TBD pending stack selection.\n- **Git:** Initialize the repository and ignore `.story/snapshots/`, `.story/sessions/` and `.story/status.json`.\n- **Storybloq:** Default setup phase plus four milestones, 20 tickets, an initial snapshot, a setup note and a handover containing requirement coverage and pending decisions.\n\nNo project files have been written. Would you like to **approve setup**, **adjust the plan**, or **inspect details**?\n\nThis confirmation comes from the story skill\u2019s [setup-flow.md](/private/tmp/cc-cpm-w4-t525/onboarding-eval-hiz4gD/home/.agents/skills/story/setup-flow.md): \u201cNothing is written before approval.\u201d It requires approval of this concrete package before creating the project files."
